    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Florence-KY/Assistant-Professor-for-the-MSPAS-Program_R3478": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor for the MSPAS Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Principal Faculty (NCCPA Certified) position for the MSPAS Program at the University of the Cumberlands is a full-time, twelve-month (1.0 FTE) faculty appointment reporting directly to the Program Director. The principal faculty member contributes to both the didactic and clinical phases of the program through teaching, course leadership, student assessment and advising, curriculum development, program service, and ongoing program evaluation in accordance with ARC-PA Standards. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Serve as Instructor of Record and/or course director for assigned didactic and clinical courses in accordance with curricular needs and University and program teaching-load expectations. Provide instruction and assess student achievement of course learning outcomes throughout the didactic and clinical phases. Participate in course planning, development, delivery, assessment, and continuous improvement. Support the Director of Clinical Education in the administration, delivery, and assessment of assigned clinical courses and clinical-phase activities. Conduct clinical site visits and student/preceptor evaluations as assigned. Serve as faculty advisor to assigned students throughout the didactic and clinical phases. Participate in academic counseling, remediation, and student-success activities, including monitoring student progress and follow-up when concerns are identified. Contribute to the design, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of the curriculum in collaboration with the Program Director and respective phase directors. Secondary and Program Responsibilities Participate in program-wide instructional and assessment activities, including practical examinations, clinical skills assessments, simulations, examination proctoring, grading, and remediation activities. Participate in the selection and evaluation of applicants for admission to the PA Program. Participate in the development and periodic review of the program's mission, goals, competencies, and outcomes. Participate in program self-assessment, including data review, analysis, action planning, and documentation. Participate in ARC-PA accreditation activities, including preparation of required documentation, reports, policy review, and accreditation site visits. Serve on program, departmental, and institutional committees as assigned. Participate in faculty meetings, orientation, graduation, and other program activities. Maintain professional development appropriate to PA education, assigned teaching responsibilities, and clinical practice. Collaborate with faculty and staff to support the educational mission and effective operation of the program. Perform additional faculty responsibilities as assigned by the Program Director consistent with the role, mission, and needs of the MSPAS Program and sponsoring institution. Minimum Qualifications (Required for Appointment) Successful completion and earned degree from an accredited Physician Assistant Studies Program. Current NCCPA certification. Eligibility for or possession of state licensure as a Physician Assistant in Kentucky, as required by the University and applicable law. Maintenance of required certification and licensure throughout the appointment. Additional Qualifications Considered Favorably (Not Required) Minimum of two (2) years of clinical experience as a practicing PA and/or prior experience in PA or health professions education. Experience in higher education teaching, course leadership, or curriculum development. Experience with clinical education or assessment of PA students. Experience in student advising, academic support, or remediation. Experience in outcomes assessment, program evaluation, or accreditation processes. Experience mentoring graduate-level students. Scholarly activity consistent with institutional expectations. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within a faculty team and contribute effectively to shared program responsibilities. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Student-Success-Coordinator-Main-Campus_R3474": {
      "title": "Student Success Coordinator-Main Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Student Success Coordinator will work to assist students in an effort to improve student retention, persistence, and graduation rates. Through providing academic advising for students and early intervention measures, the coordinator will have a targeted focus on undergraduate student success. The Student Success Coordinator will help to coordinate all student success initiatives, including the First Year Foundation course, summer orientations, and early intervention efforts. The Coordinator will collaborate closely with other members of the Student Success Team to design and implement retention initiatives, maintain advising records, and communicate with faculty regarding student academic success concerns. Requirements Candidates must have the character and personality to relate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and the community. Applicants must have a master’s degree (or at least 18 hours of graduate work completed) and at least 2 years of experience in student advising, recruitment, retention, or other related student services areas. Good oral and written communication skills and an understanding of college programs and procedures regarding advisement, registration, and financial aid is desirable. Key Duties and Responsibilities: The Student Success Coordinator will Collaborate with the Student Success Coordinators to facilitate student success programs. Serve as advisor to students and assist with course registration, academic progress, and overall student success. Establish plans of action to address negative attrition/retention patterns with the assigned targeted student population. Prepare and present retention updates and reports for assigned student population. Identify and develop student success indicators for purposes of monitoring, evaluating, and reporting on student academic progress, persistence, attrition/retention and graduation rates. Maintain advising data and contact students in jeopardy of withdrawing or failing school. Provide individual and group Student Success Skills sessions/workshops as needed. Communicate with students on a regular basis to facilitate retention activities. This will be done through in-person, telephone, mail, virtual meetings, and/or e-mail. Collaborate with other campus departments as needed to support student success. Publicize and disseminate student support materials to students. Participate in various departmental, campus, and college initiatives related to retention and student success, including outreach events. Build and maintain an awareness of current trends and best practices in retention and student success areas and integrate such knowledge into campus programs and services. Coordinate assessment of all program areas of responsibility. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Talent-Development-and-Engagement-Specialist_R3471": {
      "title": "Talent Development and Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Talent Development and Engagement Specialist supports and coordinates the University’s efforts to attract, welcome, develop, and retain employees. The position manages staff recruitment, coordinates employee and supervisor development, administers the performance evaluation program, and develops employee recognition, engagement, and career development initiatives. The Specialist works closely with supervisors and University leadership to strengthen the employee experience and build practical programs that reflect the University’s core values of Serve, Elevate, and Innovate. This includes providing responsive and service-minded support, helping employees and supervisors contribute to an exceptional student experience, and continually looking for better ways to recruit, develop, recognize, and retain employees. Essential Responsibilities Onboarding Program Development and Employee Experience Help design, evaluate, and improve the University-wide onboarding program for new staff employees in partnership with the HR Generalist and Executive Vice President for Human Resources. Develop and maintain onboarding resources, supervisor checklists, and 30/60/90-day tools that help new employees understand the University, their role, workplace expectations, and how core values should be reflected in their work. Partner with the HR colleagues to evaluate the onboarding experience and recommend improvements. Develop practical follow-up tools and feedback methods for new employees and supervisors during the first several months of employment, and use the results to improve the onboarding program. Learning and Development Develop and maintain an annual employee and supervisor training plan based on institutional needs and feedback from leaders and employees, with particular attention to service, the employee and student experience, leadership effectiveness, and continuous improvement. Create and coordinate supervisor development programs covering topics such as hiring, onboarding, communication, coaching, documentation, performance management, employee recognition, conflict resolution and difficult conversations. Coordinate leadership and professional development opportunities for employees at different career stages. Identify appropriate internal and external training resources and facilitate programs as needed. Maintain training materials and participation records and evaluate whether programs are meeting their intended purpose. Partner with subject matter experts to coordinate required employment-related training. Performance Management Administer the annual performance evaluation process, including the calendar, communications, forms or system workflow, and completion tracking. Train supervisors and employees on goal setting, constructive feedback, effective evaluations, and development planning, including meaningful ways to connect performance expectations to core values and strategic initiatives. Review the performance management process regularly and recommend improvements that make evaluations more useful and consistent. Partner with the HR Generalist on situations involving significant performance concerns, corrective action, or performance improvement plans. Employee Engagement and Recognition Develop and coordinate employee recognition and appreciation programs, including service recognition and meaningful recognition of employees who demonstrate Serve, Elevate, and Innovate in their work. Coordinate employee engagement surveys, pulse surveys, stay interviews, or other listening efforts as appropriate. Analyze feedback and workforce trends and work with leaders to identify practical actions that improve engagement and retention. Career Development and Internal Growth Help develop career paths, job families, and career development resources that provide employees a clearer understanding of opportunities for growth and encourage continued learning, adaptability, and innovation. Promote internal mobility and help supervisors identify development opportunities for employees. Support individual development planning, mentoring, cross-training, and other career development efforts. Assist HR leadership with succession planning and development strategies for critical positions and future leaders. Recruitment and Hiring   Coordinate full-cycle recruitment for staff positions, from posting through accepted offer. Partner with hiring managers to review position needs, develop job postings, identify recruiting sources, and establish an effective search process that reflects the University’s commitment to service and a positive candidate experience. Maintain the applicant tracking process and provide timely, professional communication to candidates and hiring managers. Help hiring managers develop interview questions, selection criteria, and consistent interviewing practices. Support candidate sourcing and outreach for difficult-to-fill positions and identify opportunities to strengthen the University’s employer presence. Coordinate reference checks, background checks, offer documentation, and other pre-employment steps in partnership with other HR staff. Maintain recruiting records and monitor useful measures such as vacancies, time to fill, applicant sources, and offer acceptance. Program Administration and Collaboration Maintain accurate records and documentation for assigned talent programs. Use HR data and employee feedback to evaluate recruiting, onboarding, development, performance, engagement, and retention efforts. Prepare reports and recommendations for HR leadership and other University leaders as requested. Work closely with the HR Generalist, Benefits and Payroll, Leave and HRIS, and Payroll staff to provide a coordinated employee experience. Stay current on effective talent management and higher education employment practices and recommend reasonable improvements. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Organizational Development, Education, or a related field. At least three years of progressively responsible experience in human resources, talent management, recruiting, learning and development, employee engagement, or a related area. Experience coordinating multiple HR programs or projects from planning through implementation. Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with employees and supervisors at all levels. Good judgment and the ability to handle confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities and recurring deadlines. Preferred Experience working in a college or university environment. Experience developing supervisor or leadership training programs. Experience with applicant tracking, performance management, learning, or HRIS systems. Key Competencies Serve: service-oriented, responsive, collaborative, and willing to support others with care and professionalism Elevate: committed to strengthening the employee experience in ways that help employees and supervisors better serve students and advance the University’s mission Innovate: curious, adaptable, and willing to improve processes, test practical ideas, and find better ways to support employees and the University Strong facilitation, presentation, and relationship-building skills Sound judgment and discretion Collaborative approach and willingness to work across departments Curiosity, adaptability, and continuous improvement mindset Working Relationships The Specialist works regularly with supervisors, department leaders, faculty and staff, and other members of Human Resources. The position also works with outside recruiting, training, and professional development partners as needed. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-Locations/Adjunct-Faculty---Artificial-Intelligence_R2799": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. Consistent with and supportive of UC’s mission to provide industry-relevant higher education to a diverse student population. Adjunct Faculty members provide quality and innovative instruction and meaningful engagement with our students to successfully achieve the relevant course, program, and degree level outcomes and support their academic success in the Artificial Intelligence Domain. Responsibilities: . Provide instruction in assigned courses (including applicable laboratory or work that is integral to the courses). Engage and communicate with students to encourage their course participation and learning while maintaining mutual respect and professionalism. Maintain accessibility for and provide timely responsiveness to students, academic/faculty leadership, and University staff by telephone, UC e-mail, and other appropriate means of communication. Establish and maintain weekly office hours for student questions/support. Assess student performance on course assignments and provide assignment feedback to support continued student growth and development. Maintain appropriate documentation of student course activities. Refer students to appropriate co-curricular and extra-curricular resources (e.g., advising, tutoring, library, learning centers, and career services). Work closely with Program Chair and/or Lead Faculty (as appropriate). Perform other responsibilities and abide by the appropriate policies and procedures contained in UC’s Faculty Handbook. Required Skills: Strong organizational and time management skills Strong interpersonal and oral presentation/written communication skills. Proficiency in working effectively with Blackboard Proficiency with standard office and mobile applications Proficiency in any of the following topics: Statistics, Python Programming, R Programming, Artificial Intelligence, Natural Language Processing, and Deep Learning. Required: Doctoral/PhD Degree required from a School of Engineering/Computer Science with a minimum of 2 years of online teaching experience at the University Level (Graduate Level Courses) Minimum and preferred from an institution regionally accredited by an agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. 18 graduate semester credit hours in Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Engineering, and/or Data Science. Recommended: AI courses & certification from Microsoft, Google, IBM, and other similar Academic institutions. Documented work experience in the field of Artificial Intelligence Candidate must be based in the US. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.” Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Call-Center-Representative_R3441-1": {
      "title": "Call Center Representative",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. We are seeking energetic and reliable professionals to join our team as Call Center Representatives. The successful candidates will be responsible for answering incoming customer calls, utilizing company policies to solve customer issues and directing calls to the managerial team when necessary. Our Call Center Representatives are often the first point of contact for customers’ product issues, so we are interested in hiring individuals with a commitment to customer satisfaction and an ability to make quick and accurate decisions. Available Date: Immediately Must possess good people skills, ability to communicate honestly and with tact for students who may not qualify for admissions Outstanding telephone skills; polite, friendly manner working with students Proficient in computer literacy and knowledgeable of Microsoft Office Must show initiative, adaptability, resourcefulness, dependability, and ability to take action Customer Service Experience. Excellent analytical, communication and writing skills. Ability to work flexible schedule. Will require occasional weekend work Office hours and work times are based on student needs; including availability for students’ worldwide. Key Duties and Responsibilities: Receive calls, live chat and emails from students, e.g. queries, requests, orders and complaints; Problem solve and resolve issues Resolve issues Benefits Yes Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
