    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Director-of-Undergraduate-Online-Enrollment_R3437": {
      "title": "Director of Undergraduate Online Enrollment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Undergraduate Online Admissions Director is responsible for leading the recruitment, admissions, and enrollment efforts for online undergraduate programs at University of the Cumberlands. This position oversees the development and execution of strategies to attract and enroll a diverse and qualified cohort of online learners. The Undergraduate Online Admissions Director collaborates with various stakeholders to ensure a seamless admissions process and supports the institution's mission of expanding access to high-quality online education. Key Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and implement comprehensive recruitment and admissions strategies to meet enrollment goals for online undergraduate programs. Lead the admissions team in processing applications, evaluating transcripts, and making admissions decisions in a timely and efficient manner. Collaborate with academic departments and online program coordinators to ensure alignment between recruitment efforts and program offerings. Manage the communication flow with prospective online students, providing accurate information about programs, admissions requirements, and support services. Oversee the development of marketing materials and outreach campaigns to promote online undergraduate programs to target audiences. Analyze admissions data and trends to assess the effectiveness of recruitment strategies and make recommendations for improvement. Coordinate virtual information sessions, webinars, and other events to engage prospective students and facilitate their transition to online learning. Stay informed about best practices and trends in online education and enrollment management, participating in professional development activities as appropriate. Serve as a liaison between admissions, academic departments, and other campus offices to address student inquiries and concerns. Collaborate with enrollment management colleagues on initiatives related to retention, student success, diversity, and inclusion in online education. Requirements : Master's degree preferred. Strong understanding of graduate education and the needs of diverse student populations. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with prospective students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Proficiency in admissions management systems and other relevant technology tools. Supervisory experience, with a track record of building and motivating high-performing teams. Analytical skills and attention to detail, with the ability to interpret data and make informed decisions. Commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion in higher education. Ability to work a flexible schedule. Office hours and work times are based on student needs. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Systems-Administrator_R3436": {
      "title": "Systems Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 20 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The University of the Cumberlands is seeking a Systems Administrator to support, maintain, secure, and improve the University's enterprise technology infrastructure. This position is responsible for physical and virtual servers, virtualization, backup and recovery systems, data center infrastructure, physical access control, Point of Sale systems, patching, and vulnerability management. The Systems Administrator will work as part of the Infrastructure team to ensure the availability, performance, security, and reliability of systems supporting University academic and administrative operations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Configure, administer, monitor, and maintain physical and virtual server environments, including VMware infrastructure. Deploy, configure, upgrade, patch, and troubleshoot servers, operating systems, applications, firmware, storage, and related infrastructure. Administer enterprise backup and recovery systems, including backup monitoring, restoration, and periodic recovery testing. Assist with disaster recovery and business continuity planning and testing. Support University data center operations, including server hardware, racks, cabling, power, cooling, environmental monitoring, equipment inventories, and lifecycle management. Administer and maintain physical access control systems , including servers, applications, controllers, readers, credentials, and associated infrastructure. Provision and revoke physical access permissions and coordinate access requirements with appropriate University departments. Troubleshoot physical access control hardware, software, connectivity, and system integrations and coordinate with vendors as needed. Operate vulnerability scanning and management systems; review findings, prioritize remediation, implement mitigations, and validate corrective actions. Assist with system hardening, security audits, compliance activities, and incident response. Configure, maintain, and troubleshoot University Point of Sale (POS) systems and supporting infrastructure. Coordinate with University departments and third-party vendors to resolve infrastructure, POS, access control, and enterprise system issues. Monitor infrastructure for availability, capacity, performance, and security issues and perform root-cause analysis as needed. Maintain technical documentation, diagrams, inventories, procedures, and configuration records. Participate in scheduled maintenance, infrastructure upgrades, and after-hours response for critical systems as required. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Experience administering Windows server environments, virtualization technologies, and physical server hardware. Experience with enterprise backup and recovery technologies. Understanding of TCP/IP networking, DNS, DHCP, VLANs, firewalls, and related infrastructure technologies. Familiarity with system patching, vulnerability management, security hardening, and general cybersecurity practices. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to document technical systems and procedures clearly and accurately. Ability to work independently and collaboratively while managing multiple priorities in a production environment. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years of professional systems administration, infrastructure engineering, or related experience. Experience administering VMware vSphere, ESXi, and vCenter in an enterprise environment. Experience with enterprise server, storage, backup, and disaster recovery technologies. Experience with Microsoft Active Directory, Group Policy , and related Microsoft infrastructure. Experience administering enterprise physical access control systems. Experience with PowerShell, Bash, Python, or other scripting and automation technologies. Experience with vulnerability scanning and remediation tools. Familiarity with security frameworks and standards such as NIST, CIS Controls, or CIS Benchmarks . Experience supporting enterprise Point of Sale systems. Experience in higher education or another complex enterprise IT environment. Relevant VMware, Microsoft, Linux, cybersecurity, or infrastructure certifications. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong knowledge of server, virtualization, and enterprise infrastructure technologies. Knowledge of backup, recovery, disaster recovery, and business continuity concepts. Understanding of physical access controls and cybersecurity principles. Ability to automate repetitive administrative tasks when appropriate. Effective written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate technical information to technical and non-technical personnel. Ability to take ownership of assigned systems and projects while working effectively as part of a team. Commitment to maintaining the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of University information systems. Physical and Work Requirements This is an on-site position at the University of the Cumberlands and is not a remote position. Ability to work in office and data center environments. Ability to install, remove, rack, and service servers and related IT equipment. Ability to lift and move IT equipment as required to perform normal job responsibilities. Ability to work occasional evenings or weekends for maintenance, upgrades, and system implementations. Ability to respond to critical infrastructure issues outside normal business hours when required. Professional Expectations The Systems Administrator is expected to maintain a high degree of professionalism, confidentiality, reliability, and accountability. The position requires sound judgment when administering production systems and physical access to University resources and adherence to established change management, security, documentation, and operational procedures. The Systems Administrator is expected to maintain and develop technical skills as infrastructure, virtualization, cybersecurity, backup, physical access control, and data center technologies evolve. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Music-and-Fine-Arts-Administrative-Assistant_R3421": {
      "title": "Music and Fine Arts Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Administrative Assistant works directly with the chair of the Department of Music and Fine Arts as well as other faculty in all aspects of music, theatre and art operations. Regular office hours will be worked throughout the week. Additional hours will sometimes be required for recitals, concerts, recruiting events, and other special events. There will be some flexibility in regular hours to balance out these ‘extra’ hours. Primary Duties and Responsibilities: This person supports the department by: Cultivating a warm, welcoming office environment for students, prospective students, and guests Coordinating, managing, and approving schedules for work-study students in music Identifying tasks to be completed and training students to complete these tasks Providing timelines for the completion of tasks and reviewing work when completed Answering phone calls, emails, and other correspondence Monitoring Musicwindow software to assist faculty in recruiting Monitoring office supplies and reordering when necessary Coordinating with Maintenance Staff to address issues that need attention Coordinating with Communications Office regarding upcoming events Advertising upcoming concerts on campus via email and social media Meeting with Department Chair weekly to discuss the weekly agenda. Demonstrating proficiency in Microsoft Office (especially Word, Excel, and OneDrive), Adobe, Bright Sign, and Workday Creating Programs for concerts, recitals, and music events Additional Responsibilities Include: Coordinating with ensemble directors and Communications to schedule group photos at the beginning of each semester Coordinating live streams of ensemble concerts with directors and those designated to provide video of events Coordinating recording of videos for uploading to the Music Department YouTube page Monitoring the Music Department webpage and suggesting improvements Creating concert posters for on-campus and public distribution for all ensemble concerts Keeping recruiting materials up to date and available for faculty Aiding in the administration of special Music Department clinics and recruiting events Assisting with measuring and ordering of formal concert attire Assisting in set-up and tear-down for Christmas at the Cumberlands Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree Proficiency in Microsoft Office, email, internet, and internal university platforms (e.g. Workday) Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong organizational, problem-solving, and multitasking skills Friendly and professional demeanor Compensation: Commensurate with experience Benefits: Yes Job Type: Full-Time; In-Person Job Location: Williamsburg, KY Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Electronic-Resources-and-Access-Services-Librarian_R3414": {
      "title": "Electronic Resources and Access Services Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. University of the Cumberlands seeks an Electronic Resources and Access Services Librarian to coordinate the activation, maintenance, and access to the library’s growing electronic resources. Additional responsibilities include oversight of collection inventory and cataloging activities, coordination of the Federal Depository Library Program, support for library systems and resource-sharing services, and participation in reference and other library services. The University of the Cumberlands is a faith-based institution that welcomes students from all backgrounds.  Its mission is to offer high-quality academic programs that empower its graduates to ‘seek a life-more-abundant.’  Responsibilities: Responsibilities Administer and support the Library’s integrated systems and related technologies supporting discovery, access, authentication, resource sharing, electronic resource management, and other library services. Participate in system configuration, upgrades, integrations, testing, troubleshooting, and implementation of new technologies in collaboration with the Systems Management and Data Librarian, vendors, University IT, and library staff. Manage electronic and digital resource access, including activation, authentication, maintenance, troubleshooting, and withdrawal of resources. Evaluate, select, and support electronic resources and emerging technologies that improve library operations, services, and user access. Collect, analyze, and report library data and usage statistics to support assessment, collection development, planning, and decision-making. Develop and maintain policies, procedures, documentation, and workflows related to library systems, technology, data, electronic resources, and access services. Support resource sharing, collection management, cataloging, inventory, and Federal Depository Library Program responsibilities as assigned. Provide reference and research assistance and support library instruction, programs, projects, meetings, events, and other service activities. Collaborate with library faculty and staff in problem-solving, planning, policy development, and decision-making, and participate in University committees and institutional service as assigned. Supervise and train student interns or other assigned student workers. Maintain professional knowledge of current trends and practices in academic libraries, library technology, systems, electronic resources, data, and access services through appropriate professional development and engagement. Work scheduled evening and weekend hours as required, follow University policies and procedures, and perform other duties as assigned. Support library meetings, events, initiatives, and services as needed. Serve as an effective team member by collaborating with library faculty and staff for problem-solving and decision-making. Other duties as assigned by supervisor. Job Requirements:             Minimum Requirements: MLS or equivalent degree from an ALA accredited program Knowledge of ILS systems and cataloging policies and procedures Knowledge of current library technology trends and a commitment to explore innovative trends in library access technologies Familiarity with Excel and data processing programs Strong organizational, communication and interpersonal skills Support the University’s mission and adhere to employee policies Preferred Requirements: Familiarity with Ex Libris platforms Familiarity with Springshare suite Experience with electronic resource management Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-Locations/Evening-and-Weekend-Reference-Librarian_R3415-1": {
      "title": "Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. University of the Cumberlands seeks a Part- T ime Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian to support the University Library's reference services in the evenings and on weekends. The Reference Librarian reports to the Director of the Library and provides reference assistance for students and faculty through phone and virtual communication and service channels . The Reference Librarian will also assist with developing and maintaining research guides and tutorials, resource sharing services, and submitting tickets for the Library’s integrated library system and electronic databases when the systems librarian is unavailable. This is a remote position .   The University of the Cumberlands is a faith-based institution that welcomes students from all backgrounds.  Its mission is to offer high-quality academic programs that empower its graduates to ‘seek a life-more-abundant.’    Responsibilities:   Provide evening and weekend reference and research assistance to students and faculty through the Library’s virtual communication and service channels.   Assist with the development, review, and maintenance of research guides, instructional materials, and library tutorials.   Provide library instruction and research support for courses and academic programs as needed.   Support resource-sharing services, including assisting with unresolved or unfilled requests.   Resolve library systems and electronic resource issues, including troubleshooting basic access problems and submitting or escalating support requests when appropriate .   Collaborate with library faculty and staff in problem-solving, service improvement, policy development, and other library initiatives.   Participate in library meetings, programs, projects, and services as appropriate for the position.   Maintain professional knowledge relevant to reference services, information literacy, academic libraries, and emerging library technologies.   Follow University policies and procedures .   P erform other duties as assigned .     Job Requirements:   Minimum Requirements:   MLS or equivalent degree from an ALA accredited program   Knowledgeable in providing reference services to students, faculty, and   Strong organizational, communication and interpersonal skills    Support the University’s mission and adhere to employee policies     Preferred Requirements:   Familiarity with Springshare suite   Knowledgeable in use of current web authoring tools and standards   Knowledge of ILS systems , particularly Ex Libris   Experience with resource sharing/interlibrary loan   Knowledge of current library reference trends and a commitment to learn innovative trends in library reference provision     Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
