    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Enrollment-Counselor---UCO_R3353": {
      "title": "Enrollment Counselor - UCO",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. An Undergraduate Online Enrollment Counselor coordinates admissions processes toward the enrollment of qualified undergraduate online students. This person will perform a broad range of duties to meet the needs of prospects, applicants, and newly admitted undergraduate online students. This person must have excellent intercultural, problem-solving, organizational, and computer skills to keep up with the demands of the office. The position requires excellent communication skills and the ability to be a dynamic team player. Key Duties and Responsibilities: Manages admissions process, including inquiries, correspondence, collection, and maintaining admissions data. Working with other admissions staff to keep student records up-to-date and accurately entered into the ERP/CRM database. Responsible for maintaining admissions reports, daily, weekly, and monthly Evaluates prospective student applications and transcripts using consistent standards for admissions to the University. Communicate effectively with applicants in a timely manner. Provides thorough knowledge of the University, academic departments, programs, curricula, methods of program delivery, and expectations. Collaboration with academic departments and administration on a regular basis and the ability to build/maintain positive relationships. Provide prompt and efficient customer service for Graduate Online Admissions. Learn and execute new information and data processes that are required to meet the needs of the University. Represent the University at events. Receives and uploads student admissions documents. Performs other duties as assigned. Requirements : Bachelor's degree preferred. Must possess good people skills, the ability to communicate honestly and with tact for students who may not qualify for admissions. Outstanding telephone skills; polite, friendly manner working with students. Proficient in computer literacy and strong knowledge of Microsoft Office. Must show initiative, adaptability, resourcefulness, dependability, and ability to act. Customer Service Experience. Excellent analytical, communication, and writing skills. Ability to work a flexible schedule. Office hours and work times are based on student needs. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-Locations/Instructional-Designer_R3348": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. University of the Cumberlands seeks an instructional designer to support the University's online courses and programs and professional development support for faculty. The Designer reports to the Director of Instructional Design and assists with the instructional design of online courses and programs. The Designer is responsible for ensuring that the quality of the online courses is strong and is consistent with face to face offerings. The Designer will aid in the oversight of accreditation and regulatory requirements for online learning.  The Designer will assist with the evaluation and recommendation of ways in which the university can maintain and enhance online programs.  This position has the potential to be a hybrid set-up with face-to-face office hours as well as working remotely. The University of the Cumberlands is a faith-based institution that welcomes students from all backgrounds.  Its mission is to offer high-quality academic programs that empower its graduates to ‘seek a life-more-abundant.’  Specific responsibilities: Works with the Director of Instructional Design to develop and revise responsive plans within departmental Assessment Reports for initiatives in online education, and to revise online curriculum, as needed. Works closely with faculty to implement unified course format and packaging to provide students with seamless and user-friendly online learning as they take different courses. Provides assistance to online faculty in all stages of course development and implementation. Designs courses to meet accessibility guidelines for the online environment. Integrates the use of active learning strategies to enhance interaction, engagement, social presence, and build a sense of community in online courses. Works with faculty to design courses based on adult learning principles with the use of interactive learning activities and assessment strategies to promote critical thinking skills. Provides assistance to face-to-face faculty, as needed, for the use of online teaching and learning methods to supplement face-to-face classes. Assesses courses in the context of online best practices and makes recommendations for improving online courses. Reviews courses before implementation and develops a review schedule to ensure the high-quality delivery of course content over time.  Design and deliver faculty development initiatives related to, but not limited to, the use of the LMS, best practices for teaching online, innovative teaching strategies, accessibility guidelines, universal design techniques, and onboarding new faculty. Develop student training related to the use of the LMS or other relevant areas to enhance the student’s online experience. Communicates with other university offices to coordinate support for online faculty, students, and potential students in an attempt to make the entire online education experience in the University's programs more user-friendly, effective, and seamless. Collaborates with IT to recommend and evaluate technologies relevant to online learning. Consults with the office of Marketing and Communications to ensure website addresses online opportunities and services. Keeps abreast of new developments and research in online education, and shares this information with faculty as appropriate. Job Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required, Master's degree preferred in Instructional Design and Technology, Instructional Systems, Educational Systems, Educational Technology, or a related field from a regionally accredited institution. Significant, demonstrated experience in the field may be substituted for formal education. Experience directly related to distance learning and/or instructional technology. Experience in online course development and/or in teaching in an online environment, including assessment of student outcomes. Demonstrated experience with one or more of the major LMS, including Blackboard, Desire2Learn, Moodle, or Canvas. Preference is given to Blackboard experience. Experience implementing distance-learning initiatives and/or creating a strategic vision for integrating new technologies for better learning outcomes for students. Significant experience with the integration of pre-packaged publisher content into online courses, including Cengage, Pearson, and McGraw Hill.  Experience with accessibility guidelines in the online environment. Strong work ethic with demonstrated collaborative and coordinative skills. Ability to handle multiple projects in fast paced environment. Excellent communicator in both oral and written communication Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills   Desired Qualifications: Experience providing professional development to faculty relevant to both online and/or face to face instruction Successful teaching experience at the graduate level Administrative experience Record of professional and scholarly productivity Professional Organization Involvement   Job Location: Main Campus or Remote Compensation: Commensurate with expertise and experience  Benefits: Yes Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williamsburg-KY/Microsoft-365-Administrator_R3349": {
      "title": "Microsoft 365 Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The Microsoft 365 Administrator is responsible for the administration, maintenance, and support of the University of the Cumberlands’ Microsoft 365 environment. This position manages user accounts, licensing, mailbox administration, and related services while ensuring a high level of customer service through timely resolution of support requests. The Microsoft 365 Administrator provides consistent daily operational coverage for Microsoft 365 services and assists with Google Workspace administration as needed to support organizational growth and flexibility across cloud collaboration platforms. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Microsoft 365 Administration Administer and maintain the Microsoft 365 tenant, including Exchange Online, Entra ID (Azure AD), Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint Online, and related services. Provision, modify, and deprovision user accounts in accordance with organizational policies and procedures. Manage Microsoft 365 licensing assignments, renewals, audits, and optimization efforts. Administer Exchange Online mailboxes, shared mailboxes, distribution groups, resource mailboxes, and mail flow configurations. Monitor service health, investigate issues, and coordinate resolution with Microsoft support when necessary. Implement and maintain security and compliance settings within the Microsoft 365 environment. Assist with identity management, authentication, and access control processes, including multifactor authentication and conditional access policies. Maintain documentation related to Microsoft 365 administration, procedures, and configurations. End User Support Provide daily operational support and consistent coverage for Microsoft 365-related incidents, service requests, and technical issues. Troubleshoot and resolve user issues involving email, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, account access, licensing, and related cloud services. Respond to and manage support tickets in accordance with established service-level expectations. Communicate effectively with users regarding issue status, resolutions, and best practices. Assist with onboarding and offboarding activities related to Microsoft 365 services. Google Workspace Administration Assist with the administration and support of Google Workspace services, including user accounts, groups, email, and collaboration tools. Provide backup coverage and operational support for Google Workspace administration as organizational needs evolve. Support integration and interoperability between Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace environments. Additional Responsibilities Participate in system upgrades, migrations, and cloud service projects. Assist with testing, implementation, and evaluation of new Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace features. Develop and maintain technical documentation and knowledge base articles. Participate in after-hours maintenance activities as required. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience administering Microsoft 365 environments in an enterprise setting. Knowledge of Exchange Online, Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD), Microsoft Teams, SharePoint Online, and OneDrive. Experience with user account provisioning, mailbox administration, and licensing management. Experience troubleshooting Microsoft 365 services and supporting end users. Strong customer service, communication, and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work effectively in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications Microsoft certifications related to Microsoft 365, Exchange Online, or Entra ID. Experience with Google Workspace administration. Experience with PowerShell scripting and automation. Familiarity with identity management, security, and compliance concepts. Experience working in higher education or a similarly complex enterprise environment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Thorough understanding of cloud-based collaboration and productivity platforms. Ability to analyze and resolve technical issues efficiently and effectively. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to document procedures and communicate technical information to non-technical users. Commitment to providing excellent customer service and maintaining system reliability. Working Conditions On-site office-based work environment with extended periods of computer use. May require occasional evening or weekend work for maintenance activities, upgrades, or emergency support. Ability to lift and move equipment weighing up to 25 pounds, if necessary. This position plays a critical role in ensuring reliable and secure cloud collaboration services while providing responsive support to faculty, staff, and students. Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
    },
    "https://ucumberlands.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Remote-Locations/Adjunct-Position-for-Political-Science_R3332": {
      "title": "Adjunct Position for Political Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nGet Set for Cumberlands! Join our team of student-focused individuals working together in order to encourage intellectual and spiritual growth, leadership and service. CURRENT STUDENT or EMPLOYEE? Please log into Workday and use the Career Tile to find and apply to jobs from our internal career sites. The University of the Cumberlands   is   currently seeking candidates for   adjunct faculty to   teach undergraduate   political science   courses online.  Under the direction of the Chair of the   History and Political Science   department ,   this position is responsible for teaching undergraduate   Political Science   courses.   The University of the Cumberlands is a faith-based institution that welcomes students from all backgrounds. Its mission is to offer high-quality academic programs that empower graduates to “seek a life more abundant.”      Job Responsibilities:   Responsible for teaching online   political science   courses, which include but are not limited to:   POLS 131: Introduction to Political Science   POLS 233: American National Government   POLS 235: Introduction to International Affairs   Collaborate with colleagues in the   History and Political Science   department and throughout the university.   Adapt and align course materials using departmental syllabus templates, required text(s), and other resources.   Provide regular and timely feedback on student work.   Maintain regular communication with students through virtual office hours and e-mail.   Maintain clear, consistent records in   iLearn   (Blackboard) and UC One ( Workday ).   Participate in department-wide assessments.   Respond to student evaluations.   Follow university policies and procedures.     Job Requirements:    MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:   Masters   degree in political science .   Student-focused teaching that addresses the needs of all learners, both traditional and nontraditional.   Ongoing professional development.   Strong interpersonal communication and problem-solving skills.   Knowledge of and interest in diverse cultures and populations.       PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS:   PhD in   Political Science .   Experience in teaching and/or developing online courses in   Political Science .   Experience with a variety of pedagogical and technological educational delivery methods.   Compensation: Commensurate with expertise and experience   Benefits: No   Job Type: Faculty   Job Location: On l ine     Cumberlands is different by design. Our employees exemplify our motto in the pursuit of a “life-more-abundant.”"
